<title>AUSTRALIA: Ford Australia warns against 10 pct tariff.</title>
<headline>Ford Australia warns against 10 pct tariff.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Australia warned the Australian government on Wednesday not to cut car import tariffs to 10 percent by the year 2005 from 15 percent in 2000, arguing the lower tariffs would reduce industry investment and jobs.</p>
<p>&quot;If we get to 10 percent, the level of investment would be less and employment would be less,&quot; Ford Australia Managing Director David Morgan told Australian Broadcasting Corp radio.</p>
<p>The Australian Financial Review reported on Wednesday the government was preparing a plan to cut car import tariffs to 10 percent by 2005, rather than the five percent recommended by the Productivity Commission.</p>
</text>
